(IN THE NATIONAL COMPANY LAW TRIBUNAL) Tj
T*
(PRINCIPAL BENCH) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WRITTEN SUBMISSIONS ON BEHALF OF THE FINANCIAL CREDITOR) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(RE: ENFORCEMENT AGAINST THE PERSONAL GUARANTOR DURING THE CORPORATE) Tj
T*
(INSOLVENCY RESOLUTION PROCESS OF THE CORPORATE DEBTOR) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([Synthetic document prepared for the CaseLens demonstration. It is not a real) Tj
T*
(filing and is not attributed to any real proceeding, chamber or advocate.]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I. PRELIMINARY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. These submissions address a single question: whether the moratorium) Tj
T*
(declared under Section 14 of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016 bars) Tj
T*
(the Financial Creditor from proceeding against the Personal Guarantor whose) Tj
T*
(liability arises under Section 128 of the Indian Contract Act, 1872.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. It is respectfully submitted that it does not. The position is settled by a) Tj
T*
(consistent line of authority of the Hon'ble Supreme Court, which is set out) Tj
T*
(below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(II. THE MORATORIUM IS CORPOROCENTRIC) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. The Hon'ble Supreme Court has held that the moratorium under Section 14) Tj
T*
(operates only in respect of the corporate debtor. In State Bank of India v.) Tj
T*
(V. Ramakrishnan & Anr., \(2019\) 17 SCC 394, the Court considered the reach of) Tj
T*
(the provision and concluded at paragraph 26 that the assets of a personal) Tj
T*
(guarantor stand outside its sweep.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. That conclusion follows from the text of the provision itself. Section 14) Tj
T*
(refers to the corporate debtor alone, and the Adjudicating Authority has no) Tj
T*
(warrant to read into it a personal immunity for sureties.) Tj
T*
ET
